  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened capacity of member States to ratify and apply international labour standards and to fulfil their reporting obligations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In Ethiopia, several projects are involved in the promotion of ILS application, especially related to collective bargaining and minimum wages, however with small successes. The CPO aims to continue to provide the required technical support to the tripartite constituents in the whole process from the legal gap analysis to the submission of the documentation for ratification of the Convections such as Nos. 131 (minimum wage fixing). This is considered achievable under the CPO in view of the understanding and progresses made on this subject with the tripartite partners. The strategy in this regard will continue to focus on building capacity of the tripartite partners and other pertinent government ministries on minimum wage models, approaches and implementation and likely impacts as well as sharing practical experiences from other countries.
Potentially, progress can be achieved in the biennium because of the contributions made by several ILO DC projects which prompted the Ministry of Labour and Social Affairs of the Federal Republic of Ethiopia in collaboration with its social partners to consider the ratification and internalization of a number of technical ILO Conventions, mainly related to employment agencies, industrial relations, social dialogue and gender.</narrative>
  </description>
